# Line endings.
#
# Git converts on checkout where the platform asks it to, which is normally
# invisible. It is not invisible to a file whose bytes are pinned: the contract
# fixtures are copies of server responses, their SHA-256 is recorded in
# MANIFEST.sha256, and the test that verifies it reads the file from disk. A
# Windows checkout rewrote every LF and the whole directory failed its own
# integrity check -- the first and only test to fail on that platform, saying
# "account.export.json was modified locally" about a file nobody had touched.
#
# LF for the fixtures and the manifest that measures them, always and on every
# platform.
test/fixtures/contract/v1/** text eol=lf
